/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-67-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-68-  // ==== dict subscript-assign: d[k] = v (insert/update in place) =============
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-69-  // Only for a LOCAL dict variable X (the current scope holds it). Reuses dPutK/dPutV.
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-70-  syntax Val ::= dictSet(Val, Val, Val) [function]
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k:71:  rule dictSet(dictV(KS:ValSeq, VS:ValSeq), K:Val, V:Val) => dictV(dPutK(KS, K), dPutV(KS, VS, K, V))
